-- title:
--   Characterization of a complete codimension-one face
-- statement:
--   Work in an $n$-dimensional cubical Sperner grid $\{0,\ldots,p\}^n$. A simplex is an injective ordered list of vertices, nondecreasing in every coordinate, whose first and last vertices differ by at most one in each coordinate.
--
--   Let $J$ be an $n$-simplex and let $I$ be an ordered list of $n$ vertices. Then $I$ is a complete face of $J$ exactly when there is a vertex $j$ such that
--
--   $$I=\partial_jJ,\qquad \forall c<n\;\exists i\ne j\;\ell(J_i)=c.$$
--
--   This characterizes complete faces by one deletion and the labels that remain.
-- source:
